        "temperament": "Docile",
        "wild": "Mammuthus steincaput is generally docile unless provoked, wandering the tundra and mountain regions in small herds. When threatened, they can become a terrifying force — their powerful trunk and tusks can send even large predators flying. They are well-adapted to cold climates and are a common sight in the snow biome.",
        "domesticated": "The Mammoth is a versatile work animal prized for its ability to harvest large quantities of wood and thatch with its tusks. It also functions as a mobile drumming platform — the Mammoth's trumpet call can provide a war drum buff to nearby allied creatures, boosting their combat effectiveness. It is one of the better mounts for cold-weather expeditions."
